WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.960
- [Instructor] What we're
going to do in this video

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:05.550
is explore place value involving decimals,

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.120
and in particular, we're gonna think about

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.070
how you can regroup value
from one place to another,

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.210
which is gonna be very
useful later in your life

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.830
when you start doing some
more arithmetic with decimals.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.250
So let's first think
about what this number is

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.083
right over here.

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:23.490
So each square represents a one

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.650
or represents a whole,
so what number is this?

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:31.510
Well, you could see that
we have three whole ones,

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.250
so we could write three,

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:36.590
and then we have right over here,

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.910
a whole is divided into 10
equal bars, these vertical bars,

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.930
and so each of these are 1/10

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.570
and four of them are shaded
in, so it's three ones,

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:51.570
4/10, and in this part right over here,

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:54.590
we've divided a whole
into 100 equal sections.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.920
It's a 10 by 10 grid,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.640
and we can see that one, two, three, four,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.490
five, six, seven of them are shaded in.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.230
So this represents 7/100,

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:05.840
so this is 3.47,

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.660
or three and 4/10 and 7/100

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:11.470
or three and 47/100.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:14.050
Now what we're going to do
is explore how are other ways

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:18.010
you can put the value
into the different places?

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.700
So let me set up a little table here.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.820
I don't think I'm gonna
need all of that space,

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.230
but we have, in this first example,

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.380
so we have our ones,

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.470
we have our ones place,

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:33.890
we have our tenths place,

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:38.890
and we have our hundredths,
hundredths, hundredths place.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:41.400
I have to curve up a little bit.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.240
And so what we just did is we said, hey,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.470
this was pretty straightforward.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.880
This was three ones, three ones,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.880
4/10, and 7/100, 7/100,

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.950
but are there other ways
that we could look at it?

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.640
For example, is there a
way of re-imagining this,

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.740
so instead of three ones,

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.360
we have two ones,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.120
and we still have 7/100,

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.640
so how many tenths would we have

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.450
in order for it to be the same value?

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.870
Pause this video and think about that.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.800
All right, we'll do it
together and to help us,

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.090
I will put what we had here just now.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.210
Now what's different instead
of having three ones,

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:22.280
we now have two ones,

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.520
so we could say that these
are two ones right over here,

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:27.830
our two ones.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.170
We have our 7/100 right over here.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:33.650
So essentially, we would
have to express all of this

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.400
in terms of tenths.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.520
So how would we express
it all in terms of tenths?

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.560
Well, this, what used to be a one,

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.390
this is equivalent to 10/10.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.660
Let me make that very clear.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.940
I could, let me see if
I could shade this in

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.870
with that green color, so there you go.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.960
I'm gonna shade with the green color

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.360
and then I'm gonna draw
a bunch of lines here

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.180
to make it very clear,

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.230
so I'm just gonna hand draw it so one,

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:03.340
two, three, four,

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.020
five, six, seven,

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:10.150
eight, nine, and 10.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:10.983
Did I do that right?

00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:15.400
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine, 10.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.140
And I didn't draw it
as straight I need to.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.917
They really should be 10 equal sections,

00:03:18.917 --> 00:03:21.270
but it's hand drawn, so
I think you understand.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.103
So notice.

00:03:22.103 --> 00:03:23.930
I took the exact same value,

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.910
but I have regrouped.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:28.470
I have regrouped this one
right over here into tenths.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.870
So how many tenths are here?

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.000
Well, now I have 10 plus 4/10.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.220
So now I have shaded in 14/10.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.950
That was interesting.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.100
Let's do another example.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.910
So now let's imagine another scenario.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:49.670
Let's imagine a scenario where
we have three ones again,

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.110
but this time, instead of having 7/100,

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.560
we have 27/100.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.350
So in that circumstance,

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.520
how many tenths would we have?

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.520
Pause this video and see
if you can work it through.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.060
All right, well let's get
that same number again.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.530
And now let's think about
how we might have to regroup

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.540
between the places.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.880
So we have our three ones,

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.990
so that was just like the
first case right over there,

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.200
so we have our three ones.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.270
But now we have 27/100.

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.590
So in addition to these 7/100,

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:24.150
we have to find another 20/100 someplace.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.750
Well, the most natural place
to go would be right over here

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:30.150
and 20/100 is the same thing as 2/10.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.500
So what we want to do

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.970
is we would convert these
two tenths into hundredths,

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.703
so let me actually just
shade it in a little bit.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:43.620
So I'm going to convert this
right over here to hundredths.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.250
And so did I do that right?

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:49.260
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine, 10.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.800
And so there you have it.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:55.330
This plus this gives us our 27/100,

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.010
and so how many tenths do we have left?

00:04:58.010 --> 00:05:02.010
We have 2/10, 2/10.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.170
So in this situation,

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:06.190
we regrouped two from the tenths place

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:08.200
and we expressed them as hundredths.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.250
So 2/10 became 20/100,

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:13.950
added to the 7/100 that you already have

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.800
and we now have 27/100.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.150
Hopefully that makes sense.

